{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017LRb1yrNz41WomJwWJzWjM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 01: Movie list and day picker\n2\t\n3\t**What to build:** A customer opens `/`, picks a day with the day picker (five day buttons and a datepicker), and sees the movies playing that day with their screening times, loaded from the backend, with loading, error and empty states. The selected day lives in the URL. Clicking a screening opens its seat map route. Also sets up the five routes from section 3 (screens 2–5 may be empty placeholders for now) and the redirect of unknown URLs to `/`.\n4\t\n5\t**Specification:** sections 1, 2, 3 (routes), 3.3, 4, 9.1.\n6\t\n7\t**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately).\n8\t\n9\t**Status:** ready\n10\t\n11\t- [ ] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n12\t- [ ] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n13\t- [ ] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n14\t- [ ] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n15\t- [ ] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n16\t- [ ] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n17\t- [ ] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.\n18\t- [ ] AC-53 — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.\n19\t- [ ] AC-54 — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n20\t- [ ] AC-55 — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.\n21\t- [ ] AC-51 — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3632df4e-836a-4239-9ca1-2c0c9dc67b92","uuid":"66037899-73b6-4dda-b5ed-b8737d84deee","timestamp":"2026-10-20T06:22:57.425Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/project/spec/tickets/01-movie-list.md","content":"# 01: Movie list and day picker\n\n**What to build:** A customer opens `/`, picks a day with the day picker (five day buttons and a datepicker), and sees the movies playing that day with their screening times, loaded from the backend, with loading, error and empty states. The selected day lives in the URL. Clicking a screening opens its seat map route. Also sets up the five routes from section 3 (screens 2–5 may be empty placeholders for now) and the redirect of unknown URLs to `/`.\n\n**Specification:** sections 1, 2, 3 (routes), 3.3, 4, 9.1.\n\n**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately).\n\n**Status:** ready\n\n- [ ] AC-01 — Without a chosen date, `/` shows today's screenings: one movie card per movie with a screening today.\n- [ ] AC-02 — Each card shows title, genre, runtime in minutes and format (`PL dubbing` / `PL subtitles`).\n- [ ] AC-03 — Each card renders one button per screening of that movie on the selected day, labelled with the screening time (`HH:mm`), ordered by time.\n- [ ] AC-04 — Clicking a screening button navigates to `/screenings/:id/seats` for that screening id.\n- [ ] AC-49 — While the movie request is in flight, `/` shows a loading indicator and no movie cards.\n- [ ] AC-50 — When the movie request fails, `/` shows `Failed to load movies` and a `Retry` button that re-issues the request.\n- [ ] AC-52 — Above the movie list, the day picker shows `Today` and the next four days by English weekday name, followed by a datepicker; `Today` is selected by default.\n- [ ] AC-53 — Choosing another day shows only the movies with a screening on that day, each with only that day's screenings.\n- [ ] AC-54 — A day without screenings shows `No screenings on this day` and no movie cards.\n- [ ] AC-55 — The selected day is kept in the URL as `?date=YYYY-MM-DD`; opening such a URL selects that day, and a missing, invalid or past date selects today.\n- [ ] AC-51 — Every movie-list identifier in section 9.1 is present with the exact names and values given there.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
