{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user asked me to build the cinema seat-booking web application described in `spec/README.md`, as the React application already scaffolded in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in `apps/cinescope`). The stack is described in `spec/stack.md`. Work must proceed through the tickets in `spec/tickets/` **in order** (01 through 07). `spec/README.md` is stated to be the complete specification — I must not ask any questions, and where the spec is silent I should choose the simplest option that satisfies it. The task is finished only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. Key hard constraints from the spec: package manager is pnpm only (no npm/yarn); app serves at port 4200 (fixed); do not add dependencies (everything needed is already installed: React 19, Vite, React Router 6, SCSS, Vitest, ESLint, MUI 9 `@mui/material`+`@mui/icons-material`, MUI X Date Pickers with dayjs); do not edit `db.json` by hand; desktop-only viewport (1280×720+), all text in English; backend is json-server 0.17.4 on `http://localhost:3000` started via `pnpm api`; use UI library components (MUI) for every button, text field, checkbox, toast, and the datepicker — the seat map, legend, and selected-seats panel are hand-drawn by the application itself.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Nx 23 monorepo, Nx project `cinescope`, Vite build (`pnpm nx build cinescope`, requires `CI=true` env var to avoid an interactive pnpm install prompt failure: `ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY`)\n   - React 19 + React Router 6 (`BrowserRouter`, `Routes`/`Route`, `useParams`, `useNavigate`, `useSearchParams`)\n   - MUI 9.4.0 (`@mui/material`) + MUI X Date Pickers 9.14.0 (`@mui/x-date-pickers`) + dayjs 1.11.23\n   - **Critical MUI v9 behavior discovered**: `Box`, `Stack`, and `Typography` in this installed version do NOT accept direct CSS-shorthand/system props (e.g. `mx`, `p`, `maxWidth`, `width`, `height`, `bgcolor`, `borderRadius`, `alignItems`, `justifyContent`, `flexWrap`, `gap`, `display`, `mt`, `textAlign`, `alignSelf`) — `BoxOwnProps` only has `children`/`ref`/`sx`; `StackOwnProps` only has `children`/`direction`/`spacing`/`divider`/`useFlexGap`/`sx`; `TypographyOwnProps` only has `align` (not `textAlign`), `color`, `gutterBottom`, `noWrap`, `sx`, `variant`, etc. All such styling must go through the `sx` prop instead, and `textAlign` must become `align` on Typography.\n   - MUI `TextField` `slotProps.htmlInput` works fine for attaching `data-testid` to the native `<input>`, but `slotProps.inputLabel` and `slotProps.formHelperText` do NOT accept arbitrary `data-testid` in their typed interfaces in this version (TS2353 errors) — a different approach is needed for label/error element testids (custom standalone elements, not slotProps).\n   - MUI X `DatePicker`'s default `slotProps.textField` slot has its own `PickersTextFieldProps`/`PickersTextFieldSlotProps` shape that is different from plain MUI `TextField`'s slot props, and `htmlInput` placement there also caused a TS error — needs a different strategy (likely wrapping the DatePicker component itself in a `<Box data-testid=\"date-picker\">`).\n   - dayjs with `customParseFormat` plugin for strict ISO date parsing\n   - CSS Grid layout technique for the 15×24 auditorium: 28 explicit grid-column tracks (1 label + 4 seats + 1 aisle + 16 seats + 1 aisle + 4 seats + 1 label), with per-row wrapper `<div>`s using `display: contents` so `seat-row` DOM elements exist (for `data-testid=\"seat-row\"`) without breaking the shared grid alignment across all 15 rows; each seat/couch/aisle/label cell gets explicit inline `gridColumn`/`gridRow` styles.\n   - CSS custom property pattern (`--seat-bg`) to guarantee hover/focus never changes a seat's background color (`background-color: var(--seat-bg)` applied identically in base, `:hover`, and `:focus` states).\n   - `sessionStorage`-backed booking state (`cinescope.booking` key) with a `Booking` interface holding `screeningId`, `seats: string[]` (flat seat-identifier list where a couch contributes both its identifiers), `checkout: CheckoutValues` (persisted as typed), `paid: boolean`, `customerEmail: string | null`.\n   - Route guard pattern: guards run once per page mount via `useEffect`, reading `loadBooking()` directly from storage and calling `navigate('/', { replace: true })` when conditions fail — not reactively on every booking state change.\n   - Seat/couch pricing and grouping logic centralized in `seatUtils.ts`, reused by both the selected-seats panel (grouped by row) and the summary page (flat list of items) via a single `getBookingItems()` function.\n   - Toast system built as React Context + MUI `Snackbar`/`Alert`, with the context default value being a no-op function (not `null`) specifically so that `useToast()` never throws when called outside a provider — this was a deliberate fix to avoid breaking the existing `app.spec.tsx` test which renders `<App />` wrapped only in `<BrowserRouter>` without `<ToastProvider>`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/types.ts`** (created) — `Movie`, `Screening`, `Customer`, `Reservation`, `ReservationInput` TypeScript interfaces matching the spec's data model exactly.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/api.ts`** (created) — Backend client functions:\n     ```ts\n     const BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000';\n     async function getJSON<T>(path: string): Promise<T> { ... }\n     export function fetchMovies(): Promise<Movie[]>\n     export function fetchScreeningsByDate(date: string): Promise<Screening[]>\n     export function fetchScreening(id: number | string): Promise<Screening>\n     export function fetchMovie(id: number | string): Promise<Movie>\n     export async function createReservation(input: ReservationInput): Promise<Reservation>\n     ```\n     Any non-2xx response or network error throws (treated as failure per spec).\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/dateUtils.ts`** (created) — `ISO_DATE_FORMAT = 'YYYY-MM-DD'`; `today()`; `parseDateParam(raw: string | null): Dayjs` (missing/invalid/past date → today, using `dayjs.extend(customParseFormat)` and strict parsing); `toISODate()`; `formatShowDate(date, time)` → `dayjs(...).format('dddd D MMM HH:mm')` e.g. \"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00\".\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/seatUtils.ts`** (created) — Core geometry/pricing/selection logic:\n     - Constants: `ROW_COUNT=15`, `COLUMN_COUNT=24`, `COUCH_ROW=15`, `ACCESSIBLE_ROW=1`, `ACCESSIBLE_COLUMNS=[10..15]`, `MAX_SEATS=10`, `COUCH_PRICE=89`\n     - `seatId(row,col)` → `R{row}C{col}`; `parseSeatId(id)` reverse-parses via regex `/^R(\\d+)C(\\d+)$/`\n     - `isAccessible(row,column)`; `rowColumns(row)` (rows 1-10 → columns 5-24; rows 11-14 → columns 1-24; row 15 → `[]`); `couches()` → 12 `[start,end]` pairs (1-2,3-4,...,23-24)\n     - `seatPrice(row)` (rows≤5→25, ≤10→32, ≤14→39, throws for row 15); `formatPrice(amount)` → `\"25.00 PLN\"`\n     - `seatState(row,col,occupied,selected): SeatState` and `couchState(row,colStart,colEnd,occupied,selected): SeatState` — returns `'available'|'selected'|'unavailable'|'accessible'`\n     - `SeatItem` interface and `getBookingItems(seatIds: string[]): SeatItem[]` — groups flat seat-id list by row, pairs up row-15 columns into couches (sorted, chunked by 2), sorts items by row then column/columnStart; this is the single shared function reused by both the selected-seats panel and summary page\n     - `seatDescription(item)` → column number or `\"Couch a-b\"`; `totalPrice(seatIds)`; `seatCount(seatIds)`\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/booking.ts`** (created) — `CheckoutValues` interface (firstName, lastName, email, confirmEmail, phone, acceptTerms); `Booking` interface (screeningId, seats, checkout, paid, customerEmail); `emptyCheckout()`, `emptyBooking(screeningId)`; `isBooking()` type guard; `loadBooking()`/`saveBooking()`/`clearBooking()` using `sessionStorage` key `'cinescope.booking'`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/toast/ToastProvider.tsx`** (created) — `ToastContext = createContext<ShowToast>(() => undefined)` (no-op default, not null, to avoid throwing in tests without a provider); `ToastProvider` manages `message` state with a 4000ms auto-clear timer (`TOAST_DURATION_MS`), replacing any existing toast and resetting the timer; renders `<Snackbar open={message!==null}><Alert data-testid=\"toast\" severity=\"info\" variant=\"filled\">{message}</Alert></Snackbar>`; `useToast()` hook returns `useContext(ToastContext)` directly (no throw).\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/main.tsx`** (edited) — Added `import { ToastProvider } from './toast/ToastProvider';` and wrapped `<App />` with `<ToastProvider>` inside `<BrowserRouter>`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/app/app.tsx`** (rewritten) —\n     ```tsx\n     <Routes>\n       <Route path=\"/\" element={<MovieListPage />} />\n       <Route path=\"/screenings/:screeningId/seats\" element={<SeatSelectionPage />} />\n       <Route path=\"/screenings/:screeningId/summary\" element={<SummaryPage />} />\n       <Route path=\"/screenings/:screeningId/checkout\" element={<CheckoutPage />} />\n       <Route path=\"/confirmation\" element={<ConfirmationPage />} />\n       <Route path=\"*\" element={<Navigate to=\"/\" replace />} />\n     </Routes>\n     ```\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/MovieListPage/DayPicker.tsx`** (created, then edited for sx fixes) — Renders `data-testid=\"day-picker\"` container with 5 `data-testid=\"day-button\"` buttons (`data-date`, `data-selected`) labelled \"Today\" then weekday names, plus an MUI `DatePicker` with `minDate={todayDate}`. Current content after fixes:\n     ```tsx\n     <Box\n       data-testid=\"day-picker\"\n       sx={{ display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center', gap: 1.5, flexWrap: 'wrap' }}\n     >\n       {quickDays.map(...)}\n       <DatePicker\n         value={selectedDate}\n         minDate={todayDate}\n         onChange={(value) => { if (value && value.isValid()) onSelectDate(value); }}\n         slotProps={{ textField: { htmlInput: { 'data-testid': 'date-picker' } } }}\n       />\n     </Box>\n     ```\n     **NOTE: This last `slotProps.textField.htmlInput` line is currently BROKEN per the latest typecheck run** — TS error: `'htmlInput' does not exist in type 'SlotComponentPropsFromProps<PickersTextFieldProps, {}, FieldOwnerState>'`. This was NOT yet fixed before the summary cutoff. Planned fix: wrap the `<DatePicker>` in a `<Box data-testid=\"date-picker\">` instead, and remove the broken `slotProps` testid attempt.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/MovieListPage/MovieListPage.tsx`** (created, then edited for sx fixes) — Implements loading/error/empty/loaded states via a discriminated union `LoadState`; fetches movies + screenings-by-date in parallel on `[selectedISO, retryToken]` change; builds `MovieWithScreenings[]` filtered to movies with ≥1 screening that day, screenings sorted by time; renders `movies-loading`, `movies-error` (+ `movies-retry-button`), `movies-empty`, or `movie-list` with `movie-card`/`movie-title`/`movie-genre`/`movie-runtime`/`movie-format`/`screening-button` testids. Final fixed layout props: `sx={{ maxWidth: 960, mx: 'auto', p: 3 }}` on outer Box; `<Stack direction=\"row\" spacing={1} sx={{ mt: 1, flexWrap: 'wrap' }}>` for screening buttons.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/SeatSelectionPage/AuditoriumMap.scss`** (created) — `.seat-map` grid container styles, `.row-label`, `.seat` (uses `--seat-bg` CSS variable, identical background on `:hover`/`:focus`), `.seat--unavailable` (cursor only), `.aisle`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/SeatSelectionPage/AuditoriumMap.tsx`** (created) — Exports `AuditoriumMap` and `ScreenIndicator`. Key constants: `SEAT_WIDTH='2.2rem'`, `AISLE_WIDTH='4.4rem'`, `LABEL_WIDTH='1.5rem'`; `GRID_TEMPLATE_COLUMNS` built from `[LABEL, ...4×SEAT, AISLE, ...16×SEAT, AISLE, ...4×SEAT, LABEL]`; track constants `LABEL_LEFT_TRACK=1`, `AISLE_1_TRACK=6`, `AISLE_2_TRACK=23`, `LABEL_RIGHT_TRACK=28`; `STATE_COLORS` record mapping `SeatState` → the 4 spec hex colors; `trackForColumn(column)`: `col≤4→col+1`, `col≤20→col+2`, `else→col+3`. Renders 15 `seat-row` wrapper divs (`style={{display:'contents'}}`) each containing `row-label-left`, seats/couches (via `rowColumns()`/`couches()`), two `aisle` divs, `row-label-right`, all positioned via inline `gridColumn`/`gridRow`. Couches use `gridColumn: \\`${trackForColumn(columnStart)} / span 2\\`` and set `'--seat-bg'` via `CSSProperties` with a string-keyed cast. `ScreenIndicator` uses `sx` correctly already (no issue found there).\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/SeatSelectionPage/Legend.tsx`** (created, then edited for sx fixes) — `LEGEND_ITEMS` array with the 4 states/labels/colors; final fixed version:\n     ```tsx\n     <Stack data-testid=\"legend\" direction=\"row\" spacing={3} sx={{ justifyContent: 'center' }}>\n       {LEGEND_ITEMS.map(({ state, label, color }) => (\n         <Stack key={state} data-testid=\"legend-item\" data-state={state} direction=\"row\" spacing={1} sx={{ alignItems: 'center' }}>\n           <Box sx={{ width: 16, height: 16, borderRadius: '4px', bgcolor: color }} />\n           <Typography variant=\"body2\">{label}</Typography>\n         </Stack>\n       ))}\n     </Stack>\n     ```\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/SeatSelectionPage/SelectedSeatsPanel.tsx`** (created, with one cleanup edit to remove an accidentally-added unused `UNUSED_COUCH_ROW` export and its unnecessary `COUCH_ROW` import) — Final version derives `getBookingItems(seatIds)`, groups into a `Map<row, string[]>` of descriptions, renders `selected-seats-count` (`\"Selected seats: {n}\"`) and one `selected-seats-row` per row (`\"Row {r}: {items.join(', ')}\"`).\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/SeatSelectionPage/SeatSelectionPage.tsx`** (created, then edited for sx/align fixes) — Fetches screening then movie on mount (redirects to `/` on any failure); separate `useEffect` keyed on `screening?.id` that loads existing booking from storage if it matches & is unpaid, else creates+saves a fresh `emptyBooking(screening.id)`; `handleToggleSeat`/`handleToggleCouch` implement the 10-seat cap with `showToast('Maximum 10 seats per booking')`; `handleCancel` clears booking and navigates to `/`; `handleContinue` navigates to summary only if ≥1 seat selected. Final JSX layout fixes applied: `sx={{ maxWidth: 1200, mx: 'auto', p: 3 }}`, `<Stack spacing={2} sx={{ alignItems: 'center' }}>`, `sx={{ alignSelf: 'flex-start' }}` on title/subtitle Typography, `align=\"center\"` (not `textAlign`) on the seat-limit-info Typography.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/SummaryPage/SummaryPage.tsx`** (created, then edited for sx fixes) — Guard `useEffect` on mount checks `loadBooking()` against `!existing || existing.paid || existing.screeningId !== Number(screeningId) || existing.seats.length===0` → redirect; separate effect fetches screening+movie (redirect on failure) gated by `guardFailed`. `handleRemove(ids)` filters seats, saves, navigates to seat page if empty else updates state. Renders `summary-title`, `summary-list` of `summary-item`s (each with `summary-item-title`/`-datetime`/`-row`/`-seat`/`-price`/`-remove-button`), `summary-total` (`\"Total: {totalPrice(...).toFixed(2)} PLN\"`), `back-button`/`confirm-button`. Fixed layout: `sx={{ maxWidth: 720, mx: 'auto', p: 3 }}`, `<Stack direction=\"row\" spacing={2} sx={{ mt: 2 }}>`.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/CheckoutPage/checkoutValidation.ts`** (created) — \n     ```ts\n     const EMAIL_REGEX = /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/;\n     const PHONE_REGEX = /^\\d{9}$/;\n     export type FieldErrors = Partial<Record<'firstName'|'lastName'|'email'|'confirmEmail'|'phone'|'terms', string>>;\n     export function validate(values: CheckoutValues): FieldErrors { ... }\n     ```\n     Implements exact required/format/match rules and exact error message strings from spec section 7.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/CheckoutPage/CheckoutPage.tsx`** (created, partially edited for Box/Stack sx fixes, **still has unresolved TS errors** at time of cutoff) — Guard effect identical pattern to Summary; `updateValues(partial)` merges into `booking.checkout` and persists immediately; `touched` state is local-only (not persisted) per spec 7.1; `markTouched(field)`; `handlePay()` re-validates, if invalid marks all 6 fields touched + shows toast `'The form contains errors'` and returns without navigating; if valid, sets `submitting=true`, builds `seats = getBookingItems(booking.seats).flatMap(i => i.ids)` (summary order), calls `createReservation(...)`, on success sets `booking.paid=true` + `customerEmail` and navigates to `/confirmation`, on failure resets `submitting=false` and shows toast `'Payment failed. Please try again.'`. Pay button label: `` `Pay ${total.toFixed(2)} PLN` `` or `'Processing…'` while submitting, `disabled={submitting}`. \n     **Current unresolved errors** (from the last typecheck run, 10 errors): every one of the 5 `TextField`s uses:\n     ```tsx\n     slotProps={{\n       htmlInput: { 'data-testid': 'first-name-input' },      // OK, no error\n       inputLabel: { 'data-testid': 'first-name-label' },      // TS2353 error — not a valid prop\n       formHelperText: { 'data-testid': 'first-name-error' },  // TS2353 error — not a valid prop\n     }}\n     ```\n     This pattern is repeated identically for last-name, email, confirm-email, and phone fields (each via its own `label`, `helperText`, `error` props plus the broken `slotProps.inputLabel`/`slotProps.formHelperText`). The terms checkbox block (which does NOT have TS errors) is:\n     ```tsx\n     <Box>\n       <FormControlLabel\n         control={\n           <Checkbox\n             data-testid=\"terms-checkbox\"\n             checked={values.acceptTerms}\n             onChange={(e) => { updateValues({ acceptTerms: e.target.checked }); markTouched('terms'); }}\n           />\n         }\n         label={<span data-testid=\"terms-label\">I accept the terms and conditions *</span>}\n       />\n       {showError('terms') && (\n         <FormHelperText error data-testid=\"terms-error\">{errors.terms}</FormHelperText>\n       )}\n     </Box>\n     ```\n     Already-fixed layout props in this file: `sx={{ maxWidth: 520, mx: 'auto', p: 3 }}` on outer Box, `<Stack direction=\"row\" spacing={2} sx={{ mt: 3 }}>` for the button row.\n\n   - **`/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/pages/ConfirmationPage/ConfirmationPage.tsx`** (created, then edited for sx fix) — Guard effect redirects to `/` if `!existing || !existing.paid`; `handleContinue` clears booking and navigates to `/`. Renders `confirmation-heading` (\"Payment successful\"), `confirmation-message` (\"Your tickets will be sent shortly to {email}\"), `confirmation-continue-button`. Fixed: `sx={{ maxWidth: 520, mx: 'auto', p: 3, textAlign: 'center' }}` on outer Box.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **pnpm build interactive-prompt failure**: `pnpm nx build cinescope` initially failed with `ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY`. Fixed by prefixing commands with `CI=true` (e.g. `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope`), which must be used for all subsequent build/typecheck invocations.\n   - **`useToast` throwing without a provider**: Initially implemented `ToastContext = createContext<ShowToast | null>(null)` with `useToast()` throwing if context is null. Realized this would break `app.spec.tsx` (which renders `<App/>` wrapped only in `BrowserRouter`, no `ToastProvider`) the moment any page calls `useToast()` during render. Fixed by changing the context default to a no-op function `() => undefined` and having `useToast()` simply `return useContext(ToastContext)` without throwing.\n   - **Accidentally added unused export**: In `SelectedSeatsPanel.tsx` I mistakenly added `import { COUCH_ROW, ... }` and `export const UNUSED_COUCH_ROW = COUCH_ROW;` with no purpose. Caught this myself and removed both the unused import and the unused export via two `Edit` calls.\n   - **MUI v9 Box/Stack/Typography shorthand props removed** (major, multi-file fix): `pnpm nx typecheck cinescope` surfaced 27 TS2769 \"No overload matches this call\" errors because this MUI v9 version's `BoxOwnProps`/`StackOwnProps`/`TypographyOwnProps` no longer include spread `SystemProps` — only `sx` is accepted for styling (plus each component's own specific named props like `direction`/`spacing` for Stack, `variant`/`align`/`gutterBottom` for Typography). I verified this by reading the actual type definitions in `node_modules/.pnpm/@mui+system@9.4.0.../Box/index.d.ts` and `.../Stack/Stack.d.ts` and `.../Typography/Typography.d.ts`. Fixed by converting every direct shorthand prop usage (`mx`, `p`, `maxWidth`, `width`, `height`, `bgcolor`, `borderRadius`, `alignItems`, `justifyContent`, `flexWrap`, `gap`, `display`, `mt`, `textAlign`, `alignSelf`) into `sx={{ ... }}` objects across `DayPicker.tsx`, `MovieListPage.tsx`, `SeatSelectionPage.tsx`, `Legend.tsx`, `SummaryPage.tsx`, `CheckoutPage.tsx`, `ConfirmationPage.tsx`. Also had to change `textAlign=\"center\"` → `align=\"center\"` on a `Typography` (not `sx`) since Typography has its own `align` prop. Re-ran typecheck and confirmed these specific 27 errors were resolved (new, different errors appeared next — see below).\n   - **TextField `slotProps.inputLabel`/`slotProps.formHelperText` don't accept `data-testid`** (unresolved at cutoff): After the sx fixes, typecheck revealed 10 new TS2353 errors in `CheckoutPage.tsx` — `inputLabel`/`formHelperText` slot prop objects don't type-accept arbitrary `data-testid` keys. **Not yet fixed.** Planned resolution (stated but not executed): stop using TextField's built-in `label`/`helperText` props for these testids; instead render a separate `<Typography component=\"label\" htmlFor={id} data-testid=\"...-label\">` above each field and a separate standalone `<FormHelperText data-testid=\"...-error\">` conditionally below each field (keeping `slotProps={{ htmlInput: { 'data-testid': '...-input' } }}` on the TextField itself since that part works fine with no errors).\n   - **DatePicker `slotProps.textField.htmlInput` type mismatch** (unresolved at cutoff): In `DayPicker.tsx`, `slotProps={{ textField: { htmlInput: { 'data-testid': 'date-picker' } } }}` produced a TS2353 error: `'htmlInput' does not exist in type 'SlotComponentPropsFromProps<PickersTextFieldProps, {}, FieldOwnerState>'`. This is because MUI X DatePicker's internal default `textField` slot type (`PickersTextFieldProps`) differs structurally from plain MUI `TextField`'s slot props, even though `htmlInput` exists as a field elsewhere in the `PickersTextField` types (confirmed via reading `PickersTextField.types.d.ts`), the `SlotComponentPropsFromProps` wrapper used by `DatePickerSlotProps` doesn't resolve to accept it directly. **Not yet fixed.** Planned resolution (stated but not executed): abandon the `slotProps` approach for this testid; wrap the `<DatePicker>` component in a plain `<Box data-testid=\"date-picker\">...</Box>`, relying on the spec's explicit allowance (section 9.7) that datepicker identifiers \"may be placed either on the native `<input>` itself or on the UI library's component element that contains it.\"\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved the overall architecture: a single `sessionStorage`-backed `Booking` object shared across Seat Selection, Summary, Checkout, and Confirmation pages, with route-guard `useEffect`s that run once per mount (not reactively) per the spec's explicit requirement that checks run \"when a route is entered... not while the customer stays on a screen.\"\n   - Solved the CSS Grid alignment problem for the auditorium (ensuring column 12 is at the same horizontal position in every row, including rows with entrance gaps or aisles) by using one shared CSS Grid for the whole `seat-map` container with explicit numeric grid-column tracks per column, and `display: contents` wrapper divs per row so `seat-row` DOM nodes exist without their own layout box.\n   - Solved hover/focus color-stability requirement (spec: \"Hovering or focusing a seat must not change its background colour\") via a `--seat-bg` CSS custom property applied identically across base/`:hover`/`:focus` selectors.\n   - Solved the \"couch pairing from a flat seat-id array\" problem by exploiting the invariant that couches are always toggled as complete pairs, so sorting row-15 columns ascending and chunking into groups of 2 always reconstructs the correct couch pairs — this single `getBookingItems()` function serves both the selected-seats panel and the summary page.\n   - **Ongoing/unresolved at cutoff**: Two TypeScript compilation errors remain — the TextField label/error slotProps issue in `CheckoutPage.tsx` (10 errors) and the DatePicker htmlInput slotProps issue in `DayPicker.tsx` (1 error). I had just re-read the full current contents of `CheckoutPage.tsx` to plan the exact rewrite needed to fix these, but had not yet applied any edit.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial (and only) user message: \"Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the React application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simple