 <Stack spacing={0.5}>\n     <Typography component=\"label\" htmlFor=\"first-name\" data-testid=\"first-name-label\">First name *</Typography>\n     <TextField id=\"first-name\" value={...} onChange={...} onBlur={...} error={showError('firstName')}\n       slotProps={{ htmlInput: { 'data-testid': 'first-name-input' } }} />\n     {showError('firstName') && <FormHelperText error data-testid=\"first-name-error\">{errors.firstName}</FormHelperText>}\n   </Stack>\n   ```\n   (repeated for last name, email, confirm email, phone — phone's label has no asterisk). Then fix `DayPicker.tsx` by replacing the broken `slotProps={{ textField: { htmlInput: {...} } }}` on the `<DatePicker>` with a wrapping `<Box data-testid=\"date-picker\"><DatePicker .../></Box>`. After both fixes, re-run `CI=true pnpm nx typecheck cinescope` (this was the exact command last run, with 11 errors reported) to confirm zero errors remain, then re-run `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope` to reconfirm the production build still succeeds before moving on to lint/test/manual browser verification and the full acceptance-criteria pass.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /capture/claude-config/projects/-workspace-project/3632df4e-836a-4239-9ca1-2c0c9dc67b92.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3632df4e-836a-4239-9ca1-2c0c9dc67b92","uuid":"f9d0c53e-94ba-4a85-91ca-e854615c0e98","timestamp":"2026-10-20T06:37:55.753Z","isSynthetic":true}
