{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a54dc061aa4419739","tool_use_id":"toolu_019qhPutAQhu9gtYed3XbehR","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-1000/-workspace-project/3632df4e-836a-4239-9ca1-2c0c9dc67b92/tasks/a54dc061aa4419739.output","summary":"Build succeeds. Based on full reading of the spec, all 7 ticket files, and the implementation files, here is the audit.\n\n## Data-testid inventory (section 9)\nNo missing testids, no naming mismatches. Every testid in sections 9.1–9.6 is present in code with correct names and the required `data-*` extra attributes (`data-date`, `data-selected`, `data-movie-id`, `data-screening-id`, `data-row`, `data-column`, `data-column-start`, `data-column-end`, `data-state`). Conditional elements (`movies-loading`, `movies-empty`, `*-error`) are correctly only rendered while their condition holds.\n\n## Tickets vs README\nNo ticket introduces a requirement absent from README.md; tickets are a straightforward breakdown with matching AC numbers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (section 10)\nAll AC-01 through AC-69 read as PASS from static inspection, with the following UNCLEAR items requiring manual/browser verification (not code defects):\n- **AC-14** — \"visually distinct from a single seat\" for couches relies on CSS grid `span 2` + gap producing a visibly wider element; correct by math but needs a rendered check.\n- **Hovering/focusing colour stability (5.3)** — `.seat:hover, .seat:focus { background-color: var(--seat-bg) }` in `AuditoriumMap.scss` looks correct, but actual browser rendering (MUI base button styles overriding, focus-visible ring, etc.) should be confirmed visually.\n- **AC-52/day picker \"selected\" visual state and datepicker display when a non-quick date is picked** — logic is correct (`data-selected` computed correctly, no button marked selected when ISO doesn't match any of the five), but the actual visual \"no button selected\" appearance depends on MUI `variant=\"outlined\"` vs `contained`