riumMap.scss` looks correct, but actual browser rendering (MUI base button styles overriding, focus-visible ring, etc.) should be confirmed visually.\n- **AC-52/day picker \"selected\" visual state and datepicker display when a non-quick date is picked** — logic is correct (`data-selected` computed correctly, no button marked selected when ISO doesn't match any of the five), but the actual visual \"no button selected\" appearance depends on MUI `variant=\"outlined\"` vs `contained` styling — fine code-wise, flag only as a visual sanity check.\n- **AC-56 subtitle format / dayjs locale** — `formatShowDate` uses `dddd D MMM HH:mm`; this depends on dayjs's default locale being English, which is not explicitly set anywhere in the app (no `dayjs.locale('en')` call). Should be fine since dayjs defaults to English unless changed, but worth a runtime check since nothing in code explicitly guarantees it.\n- **MAX_SEATS toast + couch edge case (AC-21)** — logic is correct by reading, but exact toast timing/debounce under rapid clicks would need manual testing.\n\n## Other direct spec requirements\n- No other unmet requirements found. Seat geometry math (grid tracks, aisle widths, entrance gaps), pricing table, seat/couch state derivation, booking lifecycle guards (routes 2–5), sessionStorage persistence, checkout validation rules (including the email regex edge cases `a@b`/`a@.com` correctly rejected), and toast behavior (4s duration, single visible toast replacing the prior one) all match the spec exactly.\n- `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds (verified just now).\n\n## Summary\nNo discrepancies found between the implementation and the spec. Everything checked out; only the items above are flagged as needing manual/browser confirmation rather than being defects."}],"resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5","totalDurationMs":104016,"totalTokens":83152,"totalToolUseCount":24,"usage":{"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1159,"cach