{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CgD31DEps6kjxhL2YhfFp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All checks pass: typecheck, lint, build, and the Vitest suite are green, and a full audit against the spec's data-testid inventory and all 69 acceptance criteria found no discrepancies.\n\nSummary of what was fixed this session:\n- `CheckoutPage.tsx`: replaced the broken `slotProps.inputLabel`/`slotProps.formHelperText` testid attempts (not type-accepted by MUI's TextField slot types) with standalone `Typography`-as-label + `FormHelperText`-as-error elements via a small `TextFieldRow` helper, keeping `slotProps.htmlInput` for the input testid.\n- `DayPicker.tsx`: replaced the broken `slotProps.textField.htmlInput` on `DatePicker` with a wrapping `<Box data-testid=\"date-picker\">`.\n- `app.tsx`: added `LocalizationProvider`/`AdapterDayjs` around the routes — this was needed for the `DatePicker` to render at all, and fixed the previously-failing `app.spec.tsx` test.\n\nOne environment note (not a code defect): `db.json`'s seed screenings are all dated September 2026, while the sandbox's system clock reads October 20, 2026, so the movie list will show empty for \"today\" when manually browsing here — that's stale fixture data relative to the clock, not an app bug.\n\nI don't have a browser-automation tool in this environment, so I verified the dev server (`pnpm nx serve cinescope`, port 4200) and API (`pnpm api`, port 3000) both start and respond, and had a thorough static audit confirm every testid and AC, but I could not visually click through the UI myself — worth a manual look if you want full confidence on rendering/hover/visual details. Both servers are currently left running in the background."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2511,"cache_read_input_tokens":93785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_